> Running 4.0d on DEC3000 300LX (aka Pelican)  have a tlz04 which hasn't
> been attached for some time.  I have the scsi ID set to 4 and this doesn't
> conflict with the disks which are 1,2 & 3
>
> thor/ROOT 259 > ls /dev/rmt*
> /dev/rmt0a  /dev/rmt0h  /dev/rmt0l  /dev/rmt0m
>
>
> When I try to use it I get, no such device error.  Do I always
> need to reboot to configure the unit or is there any other way?

Don't need to reboot.
1. remove the rmt* nrmt* from /dev
2. run MAKEDEV tz4

Help came from: Tyler Hall, Warren Sturm, Chris Eckert, Greg Merrell, Tom
Blinn
and Hoai Tran.

A couple of helpful diagnostic tools suggested were
# scu scan edt
# scu show edt
# file /dev/rmt0h

these allowed one to determine if the device were seen.

Thanks much
Tom

