From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Dec 28 18:59:41 2001
From: Peacock Dennis - dpeaco <Dennis.Peacock () acxiom ! com>
Date: Fri, 28 Dec 2001 18:59:41 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary: Making Ctrl-C work
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653644221821

Thanks to many of you who replied with good advice, pointers and head
scratching.  The solution was this:

There are several profiles that the users run through during the logon
process. Almost every single one of them had the following statement in
them:

trap "" 2 3

I commented all of them out of each profile and now the control-c works like
the users want.  I've not lost my mind, I am still living and still
learning.  :-)

