Fri, Dec 28, 2001 at 10:26:57AM +0100, Ezio Cremaschini ha scritto:
> after a reboot of our alpha 4000 (for an upgrade of the memory)
> we have a problem mounting an advfs file system:
>
> # mount -t advfs esia_domain#esia /usr/oradata/ESIA
> esia_domain#esia on /usr/oradata/ESIA: Bad file number
>
> # showfdmn -k esia_domain
> showfdmn: unable to get info for domain 'esia_domain'
> showfdmn: error = Bad file number
>
> # /sbin/advfs/verify -f esia_domain
> verify: can't get set info for domain 'esia_domain'
> verify: error = Bad file number
> +++ Domain verification +++
>
> main: unable to get info for domain 'esia_domain'
>     error: 9, Bad file number
>

It turned out that the lsm volumes were disabled! The
solution was:

# volume -g esia_dg startall

Thanks to Jarkko.Rivinoja@tietoenator.com.

Ciao
-- 
Ezio Cremaschini. (cremase@libero.it)
Jesus saves, but only Buddha makes incremental backups.

