Subject: SUMMARY: Lp jobs get stuck and do not print
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653644221717

Tru64 Managers:

Thanks to those that contributed suggestions, which include:
- Review /var/adm/syslog.dated/current/lpr.log
- Use lpc commands to get printer status
- Clear out the spool directory of the affected queue.

The solution -- I hope -- comes from Compaq Tru64 support:

------------------------------------------------
Add this line to the printcap file for every printer:
	:on=node1,node2:\

According to the man pages:
"on"	str	NULL

Supported in clusters only.  Valid entries are localhost and/or a
comma-separated list
of cluster member (host) names.
------------------------------------------------



Thanks again for the assistance.


