Dear fellows,

this morning a strange thing hits my AS1200. All at once the system went down.
First I didn't notice the fact, since the system is located in the server room,
closed and locked. So nobody may get into. I sat at my desktop working, just
want to open the Netscape Mail Composer on XP900. The XP900 froze and I couldn't
do anything. Since the XP900 nfs-mounts the users home from the AS1200 the nfs
server was not available. My first thought was Netscape crashed the Xserver,
though. But within a second my colleagues phoned me, that the servers is no
longer available.

So I went to the server room and found the AS1200 down on the knees at the SRM
prompt. The system is at v4.0f pk6, SRM is at 6.0-1, latest version available
from COMPAQ. Well, tried to boot the system and first didn't came up. Instead I
got the already known boot fail message, which I include in the mail as an
attachment. This symptom appears now and then when the system is switched on
(main power). After switching off and on the system did a regular boot. The
regular boot is attached as well. The equipment can be seen there.

While the server AS1200 was down I couldn't anything on my XP900. The CDE was
completely frozen. This is very annying, since nothing system related is
imported.

After the AS1200 was booting I was thinking I will get a crash dump, but
savecore didn't  wrote a crash dump (the /var/adm/crash has 1.2 G available). I
searched all available logs, but I couldn't get any information was caused the
total halt without any notice.

But the next strange thing is that even after the AS1200 was up again even the
XP900 (v4.0f, pk6) was not responding. I thought that if the nfs server will be
back up again everything should work without harm. I triend to connect to the
XP900, but to no avail. I had to manually switch of the XP900. It was impossible
to connect to the system. Another XP900 showed the same behavior. And the more
strange thing, nobody was actually working on the system.

Now I'm very confused what could have produced the crash of the AS1200 and why
the XP900 weren't responding anymore.

Any insight is very appreciated.

TIA


Uwe Lienig
