Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
Content-Type: text/plain;
	charset="iso-8859-1"

Original Question below:
 
There is a 32 Gbyte logical volume limit on SWXCR, and up to 8 logical
devices.  Compaq Services reflected that SWXCR is supported up to 9.1 Gbyte
physical drives.  You can use larger successfully, like an 18.2 JBOD.  If
you stripe  (2) 18.2's you will get 2 workable volumes, one of 32 Gbyte and
one of 4 Gbyte, but you must use the additional 4 Gbyte volume before you
use another volume.
 
Thanks to:
Pat O' Brian
Bryan Lavalle
Richard Loken
Alan Nabeth
Warren Sturm
Peter Stern
 
ORIGINAL QUESTION:
On a KZPAC-CA, is there an upper limit on the logical volume sizes?  ....or
on the total amount of Gbytes of all of the volumes on the controller?  I'm
currently using 9.1 Gbyte drives (RZ1DB-VW's) and considering going to
18.2's.  I'm aware that the RAID (RA200RCU, 230) has an upper limit of 8
physical drives in a logical volume?  Would there be any limit in the O/S?
UNIX 5.1 pk3.
 
Best Regards,    Blake


