to know that you're not doing something wrong !!!

Regards

Kevin Jones


-----Original Message-----
From: Kevin Jones
To: 'tru64-unix-managers@ornl.gov'
Sent: 06/12/2001 13:33
Subject: Patch Kit 4 breaks vrestore !!!

Hello Managers 

I think I may have found a fault with PK4 for V5.1 it seems to break
vrestore. 
After applying PK4 vrestore will not restore from the NON rewind device.

I can restore no problem with vrestore -x or vrestore -xf
/dev/tape/tape0 (or tape0_d1, d0 etc...) 
But if I use vrestore -xf /dev/ntape/tape (tape0_d1, d0 etc.) it fails
with unable to open subset error. 
If I mount the V5.1 CDROM on to /mnt and do a /mnt/sbin/vrestore -xf
/dev/ntape/tape0 this works fine. It appears that PK4 has broken the
vrestore command.

I have this logged with Compaq support here in the UK, perhaps they are
already aware, but just to warn everyone else. 

Regards 

Kevin Jones 



